==Icelandic==
===Etymology===
From {{term|ég||I, the personal pronoun|lang=is}} and {{term|heiti||I'm called|lang=is}}, first person form of {{term|heita||to be called, to be named|lang=is}}. Literally meaning "I am called" or "I am named".
===Phrase===
'''[[ég#Icelandic|ég]] [[heita#Icelandic|heiti]]'''

# [[I]] [[am]]; [[my name is]]
#: '''''Ég heiti''' Ríkharður.''
#:: '''''My name is''' Richard.''
#: '''''Ég heiti''' Jón, [[hvað heitir þú]]?''
#:: '''My name is''' John, [[what's your name]]?

====Related terms====
*[[hvað heitir þú]]?

